# Data Management Patterns
- We use @tanstack/react-query for data fetching and state management
- Query keys follow the pattern: [entity, action, ...params]
- Mutations are typically placed in separate hooks under hooks/mutations/
- We use react-query's suspense mode for loading states
- Data fetching hooks are placed in hooks/queries/

# Component Organization
- UI components are organized by feature/domain in components/
- Reusable UI components are placed in components/ui/
- We use shadcn/ui components as base building blocks
- Components follow atomic design principles
- Each feature has its own directory with index.tsx as entry point

# State Management
- Local state uses React.useState or usehooks-ts utilities
- Global state is managed through React Query
- Form state uses react-hook-form with zod validation
- Context is used sparingly, mainly for theme and auth

# Table Patterns
- Tables use @tanstack/react-table
- Table configurations are in separate config files
- Column definitions follow a consistent pattern with accessorKey
- Tables support sorting, filtering, and pagination
- Virtual scrolling is used for large datasets

# Styling Conventions
- We use Tailwind CSS for styling
- class-variance-authority for component variants
- tailwind-merge for class name conflicts
- Consistent color scheme from tailwind.config.ts
- Dark mode support via next-themes

# Type Safety
- Strict TypeScript configuration
- Zod for runtime type validation
- Type definitions in types/ directory
- Prefer interface over type for object definitions
- Use generics for reusable components

# Error Handling
- Error boundaries at feature level
- toast notifications via sonner
- Consistent error messages format
- Error states in UI components
- Loading states with suspense boundaries

# Performance
- Use React.memo for expensive renders
- Implement proper dependency arrays in hooks
- Code-split at route level
- Optimize images with next/image
- Use dynamic imports for heavy components

# Testing
- Components should be testable in isolation
- Props should have proper TypeScript interfaces
- Avoid direct DOM manipulation
- Keep components pure when possible
- Use data-testid for test selectors 